{"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Performance","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","type":"heading","text":"The binary-size budget"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI builds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" on every push and sums the resulting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" sizes for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStates"},{"type":"text","text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json"},{"type":"text","text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".o"},{"type":"text","text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"code":"maxBytes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","type":"heading","text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry"},{"text":" each store their running ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" in a private ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentTask"},{"text":" property, read by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In practice, a completed "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}]},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","type":"heading","text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"code":"load(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can never be observed alongside "},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"code":"store.state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"code":"store.isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"which"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refresh(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)","title":"refresh(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", but keeps any data already in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" on screen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operation"},{"type":"text","text":" runs instead of switching to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" — the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pattern behind pull-to-refresh, where the list shouldn’t disappear"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while it’s being refetched. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"duration. On success "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is replaced as usual; on failure "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is left alone and the error is reported via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/refresh(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refresh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateStoreC5Valuexmfp","text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ConcurrencyAndCancellation":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","title":"Concurrency & Cancellation","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The guarantees "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes about overlapping, cancelled, and reset calls."}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/concurrencyandcancellation","role":"article"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screens